if(window.deepArticles.mexico){
  Object.assign(window.deepArticles.mexico,{
    lead:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-n4a8d writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 -->Mexico is the hemisphere's largest independent northern balancer. A state crackdown on Catholic civil society produces the <a href='second-cristiada.html'>Second Cristiada</a> around 1977–79; Buchanan's mediation enables the 1979–80 <a href='mexican-catholic-national-settlement.html'>Catholic-national settlement</a>, followed by consolidation through 1985. Its mature order combines public Catholic identity, strategic resource nationalism, Mexican-first enterprise, deliberate Latin commercial counterweights, unavoidable American commerce, and a sovereign <a href='mexican-gold-currency.html'>gold-defined currency</a>.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->",
    canon:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-o5b9e writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 -->The broad 1977–85 Second Cristiada–mediation–settlement sequence, continued independence, public Catholic order, Mexican-first corporate hierarchy, major American presence, deliberate Latin counterweight, and Mexican gold-defined currency are established. Mexico is not formally inside the Latin bloc.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> Exact post-1941 parties, rulers, elections, regional alignments, military events, treaty institutions, constitutional form, and names such as \"Guadalupan corporatism\" remain working continuity. A later Crown is plausible but unresolved, not completed setting history.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->",
    facts:[["Capital","Mexico City"],["Government","Catholic-national order; exact form open"],["1985 strategic position","Independent under American strategic constraints"],["Public doctrine","Exact name and institutions open"],["Strategic ownership","Mexican control established; company structure open"],["Corporate order","Mexican-first, Latin counterweight, major American presence"],["Currency","Sovereign gold-defined national money"],["Monarchy","Plausible later trajectory; no settled Crown"]]
  });
}
replaceMexicoSection("mexico","position","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-z8m4p writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 --><p>Mexico remains independent and outside formal Latin-bloc membership while growing more Latin-affiliated in culture and commerce. American geography and economic integration remain unavoidable, but domestic firms hold primacy and Latin firms are invited as deliberate counterweights.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> The exact security ceiling and permanent-basing rules remain working detail.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replaceMexicoSection("mexico","development","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-p6c2f writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 --><p>The named PRI, Mexican Miracle, PAN, and Sinarquista sequence is a compatible working route from the pre-divergence revolutionary state to the established later crackdown. Canon fixes neither those post-1941 vehicles nor the exploratory chain of municipal victories, election annulments, and regional defections.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replaceMexicoSection("mexico","economy","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-q7d3g writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 --><p>Mexico maintains strategic national ownership and gives domestic firms primacy, deliberately invites Latin—principally Spanish—companies as counterweights, and accepts the major American investment and trade presence created by geography.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> Continued operation through Pemex and the precise oil, industrial, procurement, and infrastructure system remain working implementation.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replaceMexicoSection("mexico","security","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-a9n5q writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 --><p>The detailed postwar integration of armed forces, police, and former Catholic-national formations, together with the proposed ban on permanent foreign bases and American coercive options, remains a compatible working security settlement rather than fixed canon.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replaceMexicoSection("mexico","cristiada","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-r8e4h writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 --><p>A crackdown on Catholic civil society helps produce the <a href='second-cristiada.html'>Second Cristiada</a> around 1977–79. Buchanan's mediation makes a Catholic-national settlement possible in 1979–80, and consolidation follows through 1985.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> The disputed western election, lethal demonstration, named coalition, regional governments, local defense, military defections, and Vatican-backed negotiating machinery are working reconstruction.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
appendMexicoSection("mexico",{id:"historical-foundations",title:"Historical foundations",html:"<p>The <a href='first-cristero-war.html'>1926–29 Cristiada</a> ends by negotiation without removing the anticlerical constitutional order. The <a href='cristero-movement.html'>Cristero tradition</a> survives through family and devotional memory, while the UNS and PAN develop militant and constitutional forms of Catholic opposition.</p>"});
appendMexicoSection("mexico",{id:"crown-question",title:"The Crown question",html:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-s9f5i writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T22:48:00-06:00 --><p>A later Mexican monarchy is plausible but unresolved.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> A post-settlement Crown movement, succession crisis, regency, Iturbide claimant, new dynasty, and elective-hereditary model are exploratory routes rather than completed events; no sovereign, restoration date, or constitution is established.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->"});
